            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0644" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/8–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-11T12:00:00-04:00">August 11,
                            1945—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2510. Dept received last night through Swiss Legation here text of Japanese
                    surrender terms contained urtel 3864 August 10, 8 p.m. <pb facs="0645" n="633"
                        xml:id="pg633"/> Our reply on behalf of the four governments was delivered
                    to the Swiss Chargé d’Affaires at 10:30 a.m. today and text has been made
                    public.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
